==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|eukaryote|ic}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# {{lb|en|biology}} Having complex cells in which the genetic material is organized into membrane-bound [[nuclei]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1991| author=Lynn Margulis, René Fester | title=Symbiosis as a Source of Evolutionary Innovation|page=| passage=The close analogies between DNA-containing '''eukaryotic''' cell organelles and microbial symbionts require revision of classic cell theory, wrote Scwemmler and Schenk (1980) on introducing the field of endocytobiology.}}
# {{lb|en|biology}} Of or pertaining to a [[eukaryote]].

